From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bartosz Nitka <niteria@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 23:21:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] soc: apple: pmp: keep T8132's __DATA across a deep
 sleep

The wake program reloads the PMP's __TEXT from DRAM, and nothing restores
__DATA. Back up the second of the ADT's segment-ranges.

[Dylan: the range is the J604 ADT's (/arm-io/pmp segment-ranges[1]:
 0x38053d000, 0x68000 bytes, so 0x3d000 into the SRAM) in place of the
 J713's 0x3c000; our TO-VERIFY note that the ADT has no such range goes.]

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Bartosz Nitka <niteria@gmail.com>
(cherry picked from commit df00d7200e8577214e38b0439495a845e410afc2)
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/soc/apple/pmp.rs | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/apple/pmp.rs b/drivers/soc/apple/pmp.rs
index 86c19493be..b3eb8b65ad 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/apple/pmp.rs
+++ b/drivers/soc/apple/pmp.rs
@@ -890,12 +890,14 @@ const HW_CFG_T6050: PmpHwConfig = PmpHwConfig {
     sram_backup: None,
 };
 
+/// T8132: the sleep engine reloads `__TEXT` from DRAM at the wake, and only `__DATA`
+/// (the ADT's second segment) has to be kept. J604 ADT /arm-io/pmp segment-ranges[1]:
+/// 0x38053d000, 0x68000 bytes, at 0x3d000 into the PMP SRAM.
 const HW_CFG_T8132: PmpHwConfig = PmpHwConfig {
     dma_mask: None,
     check_bootargs_uuid: false,
     coreanalytics: Ep7::RetainedBoard,
-    // TO-VERIFY: the firmware's SRAM state range is not in the J604 ADT; nothing is kept.
-    sram_backup: None,
+    sram_backup: Some((0x3d000, 0x68000)),
 };
 
 impl Drop for PmpDriver {
